e model-registry-operator's\n  PostgreSQL sizing as the starting point.\n- Publish the connection details as a secret in the namespace, consumable by\n  the playground's OGXServer vector_io provider configuration (integration\n  with that configuration is a configuration reference — the playground\n  wiring is validated by acceptance criteria, not a build-time dependency).\n- Remove the provisioned instance when no playground in the namespace\n  requires it.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- When a Gen AI Studio playground with RAG is configured in a namespace, the\n  operator layer provisions a PostgreSQL instance with pgvector in that\n  namespace, with no manual user setup or external infrastructure\n  configuration.\n- The provisioned instance's connection details are published as a secret in\n  the namespace that the playground's OGXServer pgvector vector_io\n  configuration consumes, and an end-to-end playground RAG workflow\n  (ingest, retrieve, chat) functions against it.\n- Resource requests/limits on the provisioned instance start from the\n  model-registry-operator's PostgreSQL sizing.\n- The image reference resolves on disconnected installs (via the platform's\n  related-image mechanism for the PostgreSQL 16 image).\n- The instance is removed when no playground in the namespace requires a\n  vector store (no orphaned deployments after playground removal).\n- Per-namespace isolation: each namespace gets its own instance; no\n  cross-namespace data access.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **AC-1 (P0): default vector store available out-of-the-box without manual\n  provisioning or configuration of external infrastructure** — this branch is\n  one of the two conditional implementations of that requirement.\n- **AC-2 (P0): playground RAG workflows function with the default vector\n  store with no loss of current capability** — end-to-end functional\n  acceptance criteria above (independent validation is carried by the\n  strategy's validation-and-benchmark epic).\n- **AC-4 (P1): scoped appropriately for multi-tenant environments\n  (per-namespace isolation)** — implemented by the per-namespace provisioning\n  model.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":74783,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ab8e00735ca33645","agent_id":"a0c69221424ccf6a8","session_id":"afd4d759-6499-44cb-acf8-c98d0b579249","uuid":"14f765c4-6a63-4dab-a2a7-46037910bd41","timestamp":"2026-10-23T19:11:27.002Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8004 into epics"}
