{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-95f5b1b6101cf492","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-A-E004\n3\ttitle: Operator-managed PostgreSQL/pgvector provisioning for Gen AI Studio (path A)\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8004\n5\tcomponent: Gen AI Studio\n6\tteam: dashboard-crimson-scrum\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tbranch: A\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8004-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8004-E001\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: remove\n15\t  fallback_approach: If the RHOAI-controlled operator layer (RHAISTRAT-7164) is not\n16\t    available in time for RHOAI 3.5, this path is removed and the BFF-managed provisioning\n17\t    path (branch B) is executed instead; if that in turn proves unviable, the final\n18\t    fallback is requiring users to bring their own PostgreSQL by manually configuring\n19\t    the OGXServer CR spec.\n20\tai_signals:\n21\t  change_specificity: 0\n22\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n23\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n24\t  existing_foundation: 0\n25\t  open_questions: 0\n26\t  external_dependency: -1\n27\t  human_process_gates: 0\n28\t  repo_access: 1\n29\t  architecture_claims: 1\n30\timplementation_type: null\n31\tinvestigation_signals: null\n32\tai_implementability: High\n33\tai_implementability_score: 3\n34\tjira_key: null\n35\t---\n36\t# Operator-managed PostgreSQL/pgvector provisioning for Gen AI Studio (path A)\n37\t\n38\t## Description\n39\t\n40\tConditional branch A of the default-vector-store strategy, executed if the\n41\tRHOAI 3.5 provisioning-path go/no-go decision selects the operator-managed\n42\tpath — i.e. the RHOAI-controlled operator layer for Gen AI Studio (delivered\n43\tby RHAISTRAT-7164, dashboard operator modularization) is available in time.\n44\tThis epic implements PostgreSQL-with-pgvector lifecycle management in that\n45\toperator layer, following the established model-registry-operator pattern for\n46\tauto-provisioned databases, so that a default vector store is available\n47\tout-of-the-box wherever a Gen AI Studio playground with RAG is configured.\n48\tNo custom image build is needed: the Red Hat `postgresql-16` image already\n49\tincludes pgvector and is already referenced by the platform for disconnected\n50\tinstalls.\n51\t\n52\t## Scope\n53\t\n54\t- Implement per-namespace PostgreSQL instance lifecycle management (create,\n55\t  configure, clean up) in the RHOAI-controlled operator layer delivered by\n56\t  RHAISTRAT-7164, following the model-registry-operator's auto-provisioning\n57\t  pattern for PostgreSQL (the upstream ogx-k8s-operator cannot carry this\n58\t  RHOAI-specific logic).\n59\t- Provision one instance per namespace where a Gen AI Studio playground with\n60\t  RAG is configured (per-namespace scoping for multi-tenant isolation).\n61\t- Use the existing Red Hat PostgreSQL image that ships pgvector\n62\t  (`registry.redhat.io/rhel9/postgresql-16`); reference it through the\n63\t  platform's related-image mechanism so disconnected installs work.\n64\t- Set initial resource requests/limits from the model-registry-operator's\n65\t  PostgreSQL sizing as the starting point.\n66\t- Publish the connection details as a secret in the namespace, consumable by\n67\t  the playground's OGXServer vector_io provider configuration (integration\n68\t  with that configuration is a configuration reference — the playground\n69\t  wiring is validated by acceptance criteria, not a build-time dependency).\n70\t- Remove the provisioned instance when no playground in the namespace\n71\t  requires it.\n72\t\n73\t## Acceptance Criteria\n74\t\n75\t- When a Gen AI Studio playground with RAG is configured in a namespace, the\n76\t  operator layer provisions a PostgreSQL instance with pgvector in that\n77\t  namespace, with no manual user setup or external infrastructure\n78\t  configuration.\n79\t- The provisioned instance's connection details are published as a secret in\n80\t  the namespace that the playground's OGXServer pgvector vector_io\n81\t  configuration consumes, and an end-to-end playground RAG workflow\n82\t  (ingest, retrieve, chat) functions against it.\n83\t- Resource requests/limits on the provisioned instance start from the\n84\t  model-registry-operator's PostgreSQL sizing.\n85\t- The image reference resolves on disconnected installs (via the platform's\n86\t  related-image mechanism for the PostgreSQL 16 image).\n87\t- The instance is removed when no playground in the namespace requires a\n88\t  vector store (no orphaned deployments after playground removal).\n89\t- Per-namespace isolation: each namespace gets its own instance; no\n90\t  cross-namespace data access.\n91\t\n92\t## HLR Traceability\n93\t\n94\t- **AC-1 (P0): default vector store available out-of-the-box without manual\n95\t  provisioning or configuration of external infrastructure** — this branch is\n96\t  one of the two conditional implementations of that requirement.\n97\t- **AC-2 (P0): playground RAG workflows function with the default vector\n98\t  store with no loss of current capability** — end-to-end functional\n99\t  acceptance criteria above (independent validation is carried by the\n100\t  strategy's validation-and-benchmark epic).\n101\t- **AC-4 (P1): scoped appropriately for multi-tenant environments\n102\t  (per-namespace isolation)** — implemented by the per-namespace provisioning\n103\t  model.\n104\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9c0dd92e9b510fbb","agent_id":"a092b6ce1ea68b3fa","session_id":"afd4d759-6499-44cb-acf8-c98d0b579249","uuid":"8e66473c-6737-4687-8538-e0446f4f8289","timestamp":"2026-10-23T19:17:55.866Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-95f5b1b6101cf492","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8004 decomposition"}
