{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ad99c326af3c98e0","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8004-E001\n3\ttitle: 'Investigation: RHOAI 3.5 provisioning-path go/no-go for the default vector\n4\t  store'\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8004\n6\tcomponent: Gen AI Studio\n7\tteam: dashboard-crimson-scrum\n8\ttype: Investigation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tdependencies: []\n11\tinvestigation_signals:\n12\t  question_specificity: 1\n13\t  source_accessibility: 0\n14\t  local_runnability: 0\n15\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: 0\n16\t  human_judgment_required: -2\n17\timplementation_type: null\n18\tai_signals: null\n19\tai_implementability: Low\n20\tai_implementability_score: -1\n21\tjira_key: null\n22\tbranch: null\n23\tgated_by: null\n24\tgate_failure_impact: null\n25\t---\n26\t# Investigation: RHOAI 3.5 provisioning-path go/no-go for the default vector store\n27\t\n28\t## Description\n29\t\n30\tThis investigation resolves the gating unknown in the default-vector-store\n31\tstrategy: whether the RHOAI-controlled operator layer for Gen AI Studio —\n32\tdelivered by RHAISTRAT-7164 (dashboard operator modularization, currently In\n33\tProgress) — will be available in time for RHOAI 3.5 to host PostgreSQL\n34\tlifecycle management. The outcome selects the provisioning path for the\n35\tdefault pgvector vector store and therefore determines which downstream\n36\timplementation work exists. Per the Staff Engineer Input, the development\n37\tteam must define this go/no-go gate as part of sprint planning; this epic\n38\tproduces that decision as a reviewable record.\n39\t\n40\t## Scope\n41\t\n42\t- Assess the delivery status and realistic landing date of RHAISTRAT-7164\n43\t  (dashboard operator modularization) against the RHOAI 3.5 release timeline,\n44\t  in consultation with the team delivering it.\n45\t- Confirm whether the delivered operator layer can carry RHOAI-specific\n46\t  PostgreSQL/pgvector provisioning logic (the upstream ogx-k8s-operator\n47\t  cannot).\n48\t- Decide the provisioning path for 3.5, selecting exactly one of:\n49\t  - **Path A — operator-managed**: PostgreSQL lifecycle management in the\n50\t    RHOAI-controlled operator layer, following the model-registry-operator\n51\t    pattern.\n52\t  - **Path B — BFF-managed**: the gen-ai BFF provisions the PostgreSQL\n53\t    instance directly (Deployment, Service, PVC, Secret), mirroring its\n54\t    existing guardrails-infrastructure provisioning.\n55\t- Record the final fallback if the selected path fails during implementation:\n56\t  requiring users to bring their own PostgreSQL by manually configuring the\n57\t  OGXServer CR spec (a degraded, non-out-of-the-box experience).\n58\t- Communicate the decision to the owner of RHAISTRAT-7474 (removal of inline\n59\t  providers), which is blocked by this strategy.\n60\t\n61\t## Acceptance Criteria\n62\t\n63\t- A written decision record exists that states whether the RHOAI-controlled\n64\t  operator layer will be available in time for RHOAI 3.5, citing the evidence\n65\t  (RHAISTRAT-7164 status and timeline assessment) used to reach the conclusion.\n66\t- The record selects exactly one provisioning path (operator-managed or\n67\t  BFF-managed) for 3.5 and names the decision date and decision owner\n68\t  consistent with the sprint-planning gate.\n69\t- The record documents the fallback to bring-your-own PostgreSQL and the\n70\t  conditions under which it would be invoked.\n71\t- The decision is communicated to the stakeholders of the inline-provider\n72\t  removal strategy (RHAISTRAT-7474) and to the Gen AI Studio team, and the\n73\t  selected path is reflected in the sprint plan.\n74\t\n75\t## HLR Traceability\n76\t\n77\t- **AC-1 (P0): default vector store available out-of-the-box** — this\n78\t  investigation gates both provisioning implementations that deliver AC-1;\n79\t  it is implicitly P0 because it blocks all P0 provisioning work.\n80\t- Supports the strategy's success criterion \"RHAISTRAT-7474 is unblocked and\n81\t  can proceed to implementation\" by fixing the provisioning direction.\n82\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b51940858cd4c94f","agent_id":"a64b04a6e8148f8d2","session_id":"afd4d759-6499-44cb-acf8-c98d0b579249","uuid":"c138e50f-e7b6-443a-a144-a9d0bb7ce535","timestamp":"2026-10-23T19:20:03.342Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-ad99c326af3c98e0","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8004 decomposition"}
