{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-976b5bd39c25c10a","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8004-E002\n3\ttitle: Enable the remote pgvector vector_io provider for Gen AI Studio playgrounds\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8004\n5\tcomponent: Gen AI Studio\n6\tteam: dashboard-crimson-scrum\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 1\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 0\n17\t  human_process_gates: 0\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 7\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Enable the remote pgvector vector_io provider for Gen AI Studio playgrounds\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic delivers the vector-store integration half of the default vector\n34\tstore: the gen-ai BFF's creation of OGXServer instances for Gen AI Studio\n35\tplaygrounds is extended to configure the remote pgvector vector_io provider\n36\t(activated via the `ENABLE_PGVECTOR` mechanism) instead of relying on the\n37\tinline Milvus provider bundled in the OGX distribution image. The existing\n38\tremote vector store implementation is largely reused — the engineering team\n39\tconfirms the majority of the strategy's effort is infrastructure provisioning,\n40\tnot provider integration. This configuration is needed regardless of which\n41\tparty provisions the PostgreSQL database (operator layer or BFF), because in\n42\tevery outcome the provider consumes a PostgreSQL connection secret.\n43\t\n44\t## Scope\n45\t\n46\t- Extend the gen-ai BFF's OGXServer instance creation (the playground\n47\t  configuration today hardcoding SQLite application storage in\n48\t  `llamastack_config.go`) to activate the remote pgvector vector_io provider\n49\t  for playgrounds with RAG enabled.\n50\t- Consume a PostgreSQL connection secret when one is present in the\n51\t  namespace, wiring it into the vector_io provider configuration (the\n52\t  interface shared with whichever provisioning approach is selected).\n53\t- Leave OGX application storage untouched: vector storage\n54\t  (`remote::pgvector`) and application storage (`storage.kv.type` /\n55\t  `storage.sql.type`, default SQLite) are independent configurations — no\n56\t  SQLite-to-PostgreSQL migration is in scope.\n57\t- Per-namespace scoping: playgrounds in the same namespace share the default\n58\t  vector store instance.\n59\t- No OGX distribution code changes: the distribution already ships the remote\n60\t  pgvector vector_io backend (the ogx-distribution architecture context\n61\t  confirms PGVector is a supported backend and inline providers are stripped);\n62\t  only configuration emitted by the BFF changes.\n63\t- Ensure the configuration uses standard PostgreSQL connection semantics so a\n64\t  user can later point the same configuration at an external, production-grade\n65\t  vector database.\n66\t\n67\t## Acceptance Criteria\n68\t\n69\t- The gen-ai BFF's OGXServer provisioning for playgrounds with RAG enabled\n70\t  activates the remote pgvector vector_io provider, so vector storage runs as\n71\t  a separate process decoupled from the OGX instance (not an inline provider).\n72\t- The provider configuration consumes a PostgreSQL connection secret present\n73\t  in the namespace; when no secret is present, behavior is defined and\n74\t  documented (no silent misconfiguration).\n75\t- OGX application storage remains on its existing default (SQLite); no\n76\t  application-storage migration is performed.\n77\t- The playground RAG configuration remains revertible to the current inline\n78\t  provider behavior (configuration rollback) until the inline-provider removal\n79\t  strategy (RHAISTRAT-7474) proceeds — the replacing capability ships with a\n80\t  rollback path.\n81\t- The vector_io connection configuration uses standard PostgreSQL connection\n82\t  semantics, allowing the same configuration surface to target an external\n83\t  production-grade vector database later.\n84\t- Unit and integration tests cover the OGXServer spec generation with the\n85\t  pgvector vector_io provider enabled, including the shared-namespace\n86\t  (per-namespace) scoping behavior.\n87\t\n88\t## HLR Traceability\n89\t\n90\t- **AC-2 (P0): Gen AI Studio playground RAG workflows function with the\n91\t  default vector store with no loss of current capability** — delivers the\n92\t  provider configuration those workflows run on (Auto Rag is out of scope per\n93\t  Staff Engineer Input; covered by RHAISTRAT-7824).\n94\t- **AC-3 (P0): the default vector store runs as a separate process,\n95\t  decoupled from the OGX instance (not an inline provider)** — delivered by\n96\t  configuring the remote pgvector provider.\n97\t- **OQ-2 (P2, bundled): migration path to a production-grade vector\n98\t  database** — bundled into this epic because migration readiness is a\n99\t  property of the same connection-configuration surface built here (standard\n100\t  PostgreSQL connection semantics); there is no separately schedulable\n101\t  migration deliverable in this release. The lower priority reads as relative\n102\t  value, not a deferral signal.\n103\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b51940858cd4c94f","agent_id":"a64b04a6e8148f8d2","session_id":"afd4d759-6499-44cb-acf8-c98d0b579249","uuid":"57fde065-18f1-4610-9a61-7204d39bea81","timestamp":"2026-10-23T19:20:04.052Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-976b5bd39c25c10a","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8004 decomposition"}
