{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b36e8b9b44648a56","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8004-E003\n3\ttitle: Validate and benchmark Gen AI Studio playground RAG on the default pgvector\n4\t  store\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8004\n6\tcomponent: Gen AI Studio\n7\tteam: dashboard-crimson-scrum\n8\ttype: Implementation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tdependencies:\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8004-E001\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8004-E002\n13\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8004-E001\n14\tai_signals:\n15\t  change_specificity: 1\n16\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n17\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n18\t  existing_foundation: 0\n19\t  open_questions: 1\n20\t  external_dependency: 0\n21\t  human_process_gates: 0\n22\t  repo_access: 0\n23\t  architecture_claims: 1\n24\timplementation_type: null\n25\tinvestigation_signals: null\n26\tai_implementability: High\n27\tai_implementability_score: 3\n28\tjira_key: null\n29\tbranch: null\n30\tgate_failure_impact:\n31\t  action: rewrite\n32\t  fallback_approach: 'The validation and benchmark campaign proceeds against whichever\n33\t    provisioning path the E001 go/no-go selects: operator-managed (path A), BFF-managed\n34\t    (path B), or, if neither proves viable, the bring-your-own fallback where users\n35\t    configure their own PostgreSQL on the OGXServer CR spec (degraded target - the\n36\t    out-of-the-box AC-1 no longer holds and the report records that). The report identifies\n37\t    the exercised path; scope and environment wiring are rewritten per branch, the\n38\t    benchmark methodology itself is branch-independent.'\n39\t---\n40\t# Validate and benchmark Gen AI Studio playground RAG on the default pgvector store\n41\t\n42\t## Description\n43\t\n44\tThis epic delivers the validation and benchmark evidence that the default\n45\tpgvector vector store preserves the out-of-the-box Gen AI Studio playground\n46\tRAG experience now that the inline Milvus provider is being removed from the\n47\tOGX distribution. It produces a benchmark report capturing the inline Milvus\n48\tbaseline and verifying pgvector performs in the same order of magnitude on\n49\trepresentative playground-scale workloads, plus a functional no-regression\n50\tvalidation of playground RAG workflows, and a resource-sizing recommendation\n51\tfor the provisioned PostgreSQL instance. Per the Staff Engineer Input, the\n52\tdefault store is scoped for development experimentation: no strict latency\n53\tSLAs (p50/p95/p99) apply, and typical playground usage involves small\n54\tdocument sets where a flat scan (no index) is sufficient.\n55\t\n56\t## Scope\n57\t\n58\t- Capture the inline Milvus baseline for current playground RAG workflows\n59\t  (document ingest, retrieval, chat with RAG) before inline providers are\n60\t  removed from the OGX distribution.\n61\t- Measure the same workflows against the default pgvector store provisioned\n62\t  by the selected provisioning path, on representative playground-scale\n63\t  document sets, and verify pgvector is within the same order of magnitude as\n64\t  the baseline (order-of-magnitude comparison, not a threshold gate).\n65\t- Functional no-regression validation: every playground RAG capability\n66\t  available today works unchanged against the default pgvector store, with no\n67\t  additional manual setup steps compared to the current experience.\n68\t- Validate per-namespace isolation behavior of the default store in a\n69\t  multi-tenant namespace layout.\n70\t- Produce a resource-sizing recommendation for the provisioned PostgreSQL\n71\t  instance, starting from the model-registry-operator's PostgreSQL resource\n72\t  requests/limits as the reference and adjusting based on the measurements.\n73\t\n74\t## Acceptance Criteria\n75\t\n76\t- A benchmark report exists that captures the inline Milvus baseline\n77\t  measurements and the pgvector measurements for the same playground RAG\n78\t  workloads, and states whether pgvector is within the same order of\n79\t  magnitude (with the raw numbers and methodology).\n80\t- The validation campaign runs against a default pgvector store provisioned\n81\t  by the selected provisioning path in a representative environment, and the\n82\t  report identifies which path was exercised.\n83\t- Functional no-regression validation passes: document ingest, retrieval, and\n84\t  chat-with-RAG workflows in the Gen AI Studio playground behave with no loss\n85\t  of current capability and no additional manual setup steps.\n86\t- Per-namespace isolation is verified: RAG data in one namespace is not\n87\t  visible to playgrounds in another namespace.\n88\t- A resource-sizing recommendation is produced (requests/limits for the\n89\t  provisioned PostgreSQL instance), referencing the model-registry-operator\n90\t  sizing as the starting point and any adjustments made from the benchmark\n91\t  data.\n92\t\n93\t## HLR Traceability\n94\t\n95\t- **AC-2 (P0): Gen AI Studio playground RAG workflows function with the\n96\t  default vector store with no loss of current capability** — this epic is\n97\t  the verification of that requirement (Auto Rag validation is out of scope\n98\t  per Staff Engineer Input; it moves to RHAISTRAT-7824).\n99\t- **AC-4 (P1): scoped appropriately for multi-tenant environments** —\n100\t  per-namespace isolation verified as part of the same campaign.\n101\t- **AC-5 (P2, bundled): lightweight enough for resource-constrained\n102\t  environments** — bundled because resource-sizing validation is part of the\n103\t  same benchmark campaign and report as AC-2; splitting would duplicate the\n104\t  instrumented runs. The P2 label reads as relative value, not a deferral\n105\t  signal.\n106\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b51940858cd4c94f","agent_id":"a64b04a6e8148f8d2","session_id":"afd4d759-6499-44cb-acf8-c98d0b579249","uuid":"1bd531a1-9740-456a-9310-f0c5dec64d6f","timestamp":"2026-10-23T19:20:05.047Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b36e8b9b44648a56","permissio